 DM_GAMES_FIRST	switch	`=1` searches `DM_GAMES_DIR` before `dm/games`, so a provisional or derived profile wins over the game's own (the NSP script's `--provisional`)
@@ -190,6 +191,7 @@ DM_NVN_PASSGPU	diagnostic	`=<file>` writes the GPU time of each render and compu
 DM_NVN_PASSGPU_SERIAL	diagnostic	`=1` makes each encoder on the main command buffer wait until all earlier work has finished, so `DM_NVN_PASSGPU` times read each pass's exclusive time (totals read high)
 DM_NVN_PASS_SPLIT	switch	`=<draws>` (default 256, `0` off): a render pass is ended and its segment committed after this many draws while the GPU has no segment left, so the GPU starts a long pass (a G-buffer) before it is all translated; its attachments are stored and loaded again
 DM_NVN_PASS_SPLIT_MAX	switch	`=<n>` (default 2, `0` no limit): the most splits of one render pass (`DM_NVN_PASS_SPLIT`), as each stores and loads its attachments
+DM_NVN_PAUSE_WARM	switch	`0` lets the GPU power down while the game presents nothing (a pause); by default on the Mac a 64-byte fill twice a second keeps it powered for up to 2 minutes, so the first frame after a pause does not wait for it
 DM_NVN_POOL_CHUNKS	switch	`0` wraps a memory pool of 512 MB or more whole in one buffer, as before; by default it is wrapped in overlapping 16 MB chunks made as draws reach them, so only the parts in use are wired
